{"content":[{"c":["GERA"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. One of Benjamin’s sons (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.21","r":"Gen.46.21","rawR":"Gen.46.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.21","value":"Gen.46.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 46:21"},"). The name, however, does not appear in a similar list in ",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.38-41","r":"Num.26.38-41","rawR":"Num.26.38-41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.38-41","value":"Num.26.38-41"}],"t":"ref","v":"Numbers 26:38-41"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Father of the judge Ehud (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.3.15","r":"Judg.3.15","rawR":"Judg.3.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.3.15","value":"Judg.3.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 3:15"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Shimei’s father. Shimei cursed and threw stones at David during Absalom’s rebellion; later, he sought David’s pardon (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.16.5","r":"2Sam.16.5","rawR":"2Sam.16.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.16.5","value":"2Sam.16.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 16:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.19.16-18","r":"2Sam.19.16-18","rawR":"2Sam.19.16-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.19.16-18","value":"2Sam.19.16-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:16-18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.2.8","r":"1Kgs.2.8","rawR":"1Kgs.2.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.2.8","value":"1Kgs.2.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 2:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Bela’s son from Benjamin’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.3,5","r":"1Chr.8.3,5","rawR":"1Chr.8.3,5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.3,5","value":"1Chr.8.3,5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:3, 5"},"); alternately called Heglam in verse ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.7","r":"1Chr.8.7","rawR":"1Chr.8.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.7","value":"1Chr.8.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"7"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Gera","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 46:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_wor